### WordPress, Wix or Squarespace?

Website builders like Wix and Squarespace are a reasonable choice if you want to build and look after a simple site yourself. WordPress makes more sense when you want a site built around your services and the areas you cover, with full control over pages, structure and on-page SEO, and the freedom to change host or developer later. If you'd rather not deal with the technical side at all, our [pay-monthly websites for Cardiff](/managed-starter-websites-cardiff/) are £20, £35 or £50 a month including VAT, with a 6-month minimum term.

### Looking after a WordPress site

WordPress, themes and plugins need regular updates, and out-of-date plugins are a common cause of hacked websites. If you own your site, our hosting is £25 a month or £250 a year, including VAT, with UK servers, SSL, Cloudflare CDN and daily backups. Our [website maintenance for Cardiff businesses](/website-maintenance-cardiff/) adds weekly updates, security scans, one-click restores and uptime monitoring. The plans and prices are in the aftercare table above.

