Yes — we build custom ecommerce stores using Shopify, WooCommerce, and SureCart. See our [ecommerce web design Cardiff](/ecommerce-web-design-cardiff/) page for more details.

**How much does web design in Cardiff cost?**

Our WordPress web design service starts from £199 for a one-page website, and multi-page sites start from £600 including VAT. We also offer managed monthly website packages from £20/month inc. VAT for smaller starter sites. The right option depends on how many pages you need, whether you need copywriting, and whether you want SEO support included.

**Can you build an affordable Cardiff website that still ranks?**

Yes. The budget affects the scope, not the foundations. Even a smaller website should have clear headings, fast loading, proper page titles, local wording, and a structure that makes sense to Google.

**Do you build websites for Cardiff trades and service businesses?**

Yes. We work with trades, professional services, local service businesses, ecommerce brands, and start-ups across Cardiff. The page structure is planned around the services and areas that matter most to your business.

**What does website maintenance cost after launch?**

Our maintenance plans are £50 a month (Essential), £75 a month (Growth, which adds 1 page plus 1 case study or blog post each month) and £99 a month (Pro, with ongoing SEO health checks). All prices include VAT. See our [website maintenance packages](/services/website-maintenance-packages/).

**Do I need a contract for SEO?**

No. Our local SEO for Cardiff businesses starts from £200 a month including VAT, with no contract. See [SEO Cardiff](/seo-cardiff/).

**Do you build websites on WordPress?**

Yes. We build on WordPress using the Bricks builder, so your text and images stay editable and the site can grow with new pages later without starting again. One-page WordPress websites start from £199, multi-page WordPress websites start from £600, and WooCommerce or SureCart online shops start from £800. All prices include VAT.

**Should a Cardiff small business choose WordPress, Wix or Squarespace?**

Wix and Squarespace suit people who want to build and look after a simple site themselves. WordPress suits businesses that want a site built around their services, with full control over pages, structure and on-page SEO, and the freedom to move host or developer later. If you plan to do it all yourself, a builder may be enough. If you want it built properly and to keep growing, WordPress is usually the better fit.

**Who keeps my WordPress site updated and secure?**

WordPress, themes and plugins need regular updates, and out-of-date plugins are a common cause of hacked websites. If you own your site, you can do this yourself or choose one of our maintenance plans, which include weekly core, theme and plugin updates, security scans, daily cloud backups with one-click restore and uptime monitoring. On a pay-monthly website, updates, security patches and technical management are already included.

**How much is hosting for a WordPress website I own?**

Our standalone hosting is £25 a month or £250 a year, including VAT. It includes UK-based hosting, an SSL certificate, Cloudflare CDN and daily backups. Pay-monthly websites include hosting in the monthly price.

**Do I own my website?**

If you choose a one-off build, such as a one-page WordPress website from £199, you own the website. With a pay-monthly website from £20 a month you don't own the website itself, but your domain is registered in your name, and if you leave you keep your domain and your text and photos.

**Is there a minimum term on your pay-monthly websites?**

Yes. Pay-monthly websites cost £20, £35 or £50 a month including VAT, with no upfront cost. There is a minimum 6-month term, after which they roll monthly and can be cancelled with 30 days' notice.

**Who will design and build my website?**

Nathan Constance, who founded NC Digital in 2025 and has worked as a web developer for more than 11 years, builds your website. Ben, our graphic designer, works on the design and branding. You deal with them directly, with no account managers in between.

